          "id": "1771994591966",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771994591968_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given appointment/opportunity data. Produce a markdown response using only headings H4 (####) and above (no H5/H6 or lower). Follow this exact structure and formatting:\n\nInput: {{$context.$nodes.FILTER_THE_SELECTED_APPOINTMENT.$output.result}} \n\n\n- Section 1: #### Overview\n  - Bulleted list with:\n    - Subject: <Subject>\n    - Customer: <CustomerAccount.PartyUniqueName>\n    - Opportunity: <OpportunityId.Name>\n\n- Section 2: #### Opportunity Summary\n  - If OpportunitySummary is available, include its text as normal paragraph content under this heading.\n  - If not available, omit this section entirely.\n\n- Section 3: #### Attendees\n  - Create bullet points in this order:\n    - For each team resource in ListOfResourceForTheTeam:\n      - <PartyName> (<EmailAddress>)  [If EmailAddress missing, omit the parentheses entirely.]\n    - Then list each contact from ListOfContacts:\n      - <ContactFullName> (<EmailAddress>)  [If EmailAddress missing, omit the parentheses entirely.]\n  - If no contacts are available in ListOfContacts, add a single bullet: No Contact available for the appointment.\n- Section 4: #### Talking points\n  - add a single bullet: No Talking Point available for the appointment.\n\nRules:\n- Use only H4 (####) headings for sections; no other heading levels.\n- For all bullet items, use a single dash followed by a space (“- ”).\n- Do not include empty fields; if a value is missing, omit that specific bullet or parenthetical as instructed.\n- Preserve the order: Overview, Opportunity Summary (only if available), Attendees.\n- Do not add any extra sections, commentary, or formatting beyond what’s specified."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "dataPipeline": {
              "rootNode": "start_1776023732155",
              "pipelineNodes": [
                {
